              'Ready queue: tickets moved to Staging are scheduled for the next Tuesday at 9:00 if they’re ready.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'recipe recipes cross-post hashtag ready queue quick start template',
      },
      {
        id: 'auto-test',
        title: 'Test, run and review',
        doing: 'See what a rule would do before it does anything.',
        slot: 'automations',
        shotAlt: 'An Automation rule card with Run on Existing Videos and the Activity log.',
        steps: [
          'In a rule, <strong>Test this rule on a video</strong> shows whether it would run and what it would write.',
          '<strong>Run on Existing Videos…</strong> applies it to videos already on the Board, after showing how many match.',
          '<strong>Activity</strong> lists everything rules did, newest first.',
        ],
        expect: 'Nothing changes until you save a rule and it runs.',
        keywords: 'test run existing activity log what happened automations',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'accounts-signin',
    number: '05',
    title: 'Accounts & Sign-in',
    blurb: 'Understand automatic vs. manual handoff, connect YouTube with Google or your own project, and schedule safely.',
    badge: '4 guides',
    guides: [
      {
        id: 'publish-which',
        title: 'Where Reelay posts',
        doing: 'Know what Reelay can post for you, and what you post.',
        slot: 'accounts',
        shotAlt: 'The Accounts page showing six equal platform cards and the Snapchat hand-off strip.',
        steps: [
          'Connect the accounts you post to on <strong>Accounts</strong>.',
          'Turn on Bluesky, Threads or Facebook under <strong>Settings → Automatic posting</strong> if you want Reelay to post there.',
          'Everything else, Reelay prepares and you post in that platform’s own app.',
        ],
        expect: 'Every ticket always holds ready-to-paste text for every platform, so you can always post by hand.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'Why TikTok and Instagram are by hand',
            lines: [
              'TikTok only allows automatic posting from developer apps it has approved, and Instagram needs an approved Meta app. Signing in to them (where available) attaches your account.',
              'Downloading, preparing captions, readiness, automations and copying all work locally without connecting anything.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'platforms which automatic manual by hand youtube tiktok instagram bluesky threads facebook snapchat post publish',
      },
      {
        id: 'accounts-connect',
        aliases: ['connecting-youtube', 'youtube-setup'],
        title: 'Connect an account (YouTube, Google Cloud & social sign-ins)',
        doing: 'Let Reelay post to a platform for this profile.',
        slot: 'accounts',
        shotAlt: 'The Accounts page showing YouTube Connected, Advanced Setup, and 3 of 6 connected.',
        steps: [
          'On YouTube’s card, click <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> and sign in in your browser.',
          'Or use <strong>Advanced Setup… → Set Up YouTube…</strong> to connect through your own free Google Cloud project (create project, enable YouTube Data API v3, set External consent screen with test users, create a Desktop app client ID, and paste or load JSON).',
          'Bluesky connects with an <strong>App Password</strong>, a separate password just for Reelay.',
          'Threads and Facebook use their sign-in when available, or your own Meta app’s token.',
        ],
        expect: 'The card says Connected, and the count at the top goes up.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'YouTube with your own Google project (3 limits)',
            lines: [
              'Private until audited: uploads from a project that hasn’t passed YouTube’s free API compliance audit stay private, so scheduled videos won’t go public. Reelay flags it on the card.',
              'Weekly sign-in: while your project is in Testing mode, Google expires sign-ins every 7 days.',
              'Daily quota: YouTube’s default API quota caps uploads per day until you request more.',
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Disconnecting & Keychain security',
            lines: [
              'Disconnect removes the account from the profile and revokes access where the platform allows it (Google, TikTok, Facebook).',
              'Passwords and tokens are kept in your Mac’s Keychain, never in files or SQLite.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'connect account sign in login google youtube bluesky app password threads facebook meta token disconnect keychain advanced setup connecting-youtube youtube-setup',
      },
      {
        id: 'publish-schedule',
        title: 'Schedule or publish',
        doing: 'Post a ready video from Reelay, now or later.',
        slot: 'command-center',
        shotAlt: 'The Command Center showing the readiness checklist, platform states, and Schedule button.',
        steps: [
          'Under <strong>Platforms</strong>, set the platforms it’s going to <strong>Preparing</strong>.',
          'In <strong>Post automatically</strong>, choose the channel and who can see it.',
          'Choose <strong>Publish as soon as it’s uploaded</strong> or <strong>Schedule for a date and time</strong>.',
          'Check the summary line above the buttons, then click <strong>Publish Now</strong> or <strong>Schedule</strong>.',
        ],
        expect: 'YouTube and Facebook get the video now and publish it at your time, even if Reelay is closed. Bluesky and Threads are posted by Reelay at the time, so it must be running then.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'If Reelay is interrupted',
            lines: [
              'Every send is written down before it starts. Closing Reelay during a YouTube upload pauses it; it carries on next time.',
              'If Reelay can’t tell whether a post went out, it never guesses or double-posts: it asks Try Again, It Was Posted or Cancel It.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'schedule publish post now later time date upload youtube private public unlisted interrupted check youtube',
      },
      {
        id: 'publish-by-hand',
        title: 'Post by hand (TikTok, Instagram & Snapchat hand-off)',
        doing: 'Hand off a ready video and its caption to TikTok or Instagram in their own uploader.',
        slot: 'command-center',
        shotAlt: 'The Command Center showing TikTok caption copy and hand-off controls.',
        steps: [
          'In the ticket’s <strong>Platforms</strong>, click <strong>Publish…</strong> next to TikTok or Instagram.',
          'Reelay checks the video file and the caption.',
          '<strong>Copy Caption, Open TikTok &amp; Show Video</strong> copies the caption, opens the upload page and shows the file in Finder.',
          'Post it there, then paste the post’s link back and click <strong>Record as Published</strong>.',
        ],
        expect: 'Reelay saves the link and the time, and the card moves on.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'Snapchat & manual marks',
            lines: [
              'For Snapchat, copy the caption from the ticket and post Spotlight from the Snapchat app.',
              'Already posted? Set the platform’s row to Posted, or right-click the card and choose Mark as Posted….',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'manual by hand tiktok instagram snapchat publish prepare copy caption uploader record link posted',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'video-player',
    number: '06',
    title: 'Video Player',
    blurb: 'Watch local videos beside your copy, generate 4K preview copies, understand local SQLite storage, and fix common issues.',
    badge: '3 guides',
    guides: [
      {
        id: 'library-player',
        title: 'Watch a video & keyboard shortcuts',
        doing: 'Play a downloaded video right in Reelay.',
        slot: 'command-center',
        shotAlt: 'The video player at the top of the right-hand side panel above the ticket.',
        steps: [
          'Select a downloaded video; it plays at the top of the side panel.',
          'Press <strong>Space</strong> to play or pause. <strong>J</strong> and <strong>L</strong> skip 10 seconds, the arrow keys skip 5, and <strong>M</strong> mutes.',
          'The buttons beside the bar change the speed, loop, or open it in its own window or QuickTime.',
        ],
        expect: 'The side panel only opens when something is selected. It shows the cover until you press play, never autoplays, and closes with ✕ or Esc.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'If a 4K video won’t play',
            lines: [
              'Often a 4K YouTube video (VP9/AV1). Click Make a Preview Copy: Reelay makes a small H.264 copy in the background that plays smoothly.',
              'The original file is never changed, and preview copies are cleaned up automatically.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'play watch player video preview speed loop quicktime keyboard shortcuts 4k won’t play space mute',
      },
      {
        id: 'privacy-local',
        title: 'Where your data lives (Local SQLite & Keychain)',
        doing: 'Reelay keeps your work on this Mac.',
        slot: 'agents-settings',
        shotAlt: 'Settings showing local configuration and security controls.',
        steps: [
          `<strong>Videos</strong>: the folder under Where videos go, in Download Settings (by default <code>${DATA_PATHS.library}</code>).`,
          `<strong>Database</strong>: one local SQLite file (<code>${DATA_PATHS.dbName}</code> in <code>${DATA_PATHS.mac}</code>), shown at the top of <strong>Settings → Data</strong>.`,
          `<strong>Caches and logs</strong>: <strong>Settings → Open Data Folder</strong> and <strong>Open Logs</strong> (<code>${DATA_PATHS.logs}</code>).`,
          '<strong>Passwords and tokens</strong>: your Mac’s Keychain.',
        ],
        expect: 'Reelay has no cloud of its own: it doesn’t sync or back up your work anywhere.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'When Reelay goes online',
            lines: [
              'Only to do what you ask: list and download videos, sign in to and post on the platforms you connect, look up tagged products, read a Google Sheets link you import, and fetch YouTube search suggestions when you ask for SEO help.',
              'Writing help runs on this computer and sends nothing anywhere.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'privacy data local where stored storage files folder database sqlite reelay.db keychain backup offline',
      },
      {
        id: 'trouble',
        title: 'Fix common problems',
        doing: 'Quick fixes for the problems people hit most.',
        slot: 'board',
        shotAlt: 'The Board showing status indicators on video tickets.',
        steps: [
          '<strong>“This account is private” or Instagram lists nothing</strong>: set <strong>Use browser sign-in</strong> (the gear on the Library) to a browser where you’re signed in, then try again.',
          '<strong>YouTube says you’re signed out</strong>: click <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> again. With your own project in Testing, this happens weekly.',
          '<strong>Scheduled YouTube videos stay private</strong>: your Google project hasn’t passed YouTube’s audit yet.',
          '<strong>A video won’t play</strong>: click <strong>Make a Preview Copy</strong>.',
        ],
        expect: 'Still stuck? Settings → Open Logs has the diagnostic details to share.',
        details: [
          {
            title: 'A post shows ⚠ Interrupted',
            lines: [
              'Reelay stopped mid-send and won’t guess whether it went out. Open the ticket and choose Try Again, It Was Posted (paste the link) or Cancel It.',
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Built-in environment self-test',
            lines: [
              'Run /Applications/Reelay.app/Contents/MacOS/Reelay --self-test in Terminal to verify yt-dlp, ffmpeg, Keychain, SQLite FTS5, and the player without opening a window.',
            ],
          },
        ],
        keywords: 'troubleshooting problem error fix broken private instagram signed out youtube private won’t play interrupted logs help stuck self-test',
      },
    ],
  },
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Where are my videos and my database?', a: `<p>Videos go into the library folder you choose, by default <code>${DATA_PATHS.library}</code>. Everything else is in one database, <code>${DATA_PATHS.dbName}</code>, in <code>${DATA_PATHS.mac}</code>. You can move the database under <strong>Settings → Data</strong>.</p>` },
  { q: 'Where do transcripts come from?', a: '<p>From the original post’s own captions: the creator’s subtitles first, otherwise the platform’s automatic captions. Use <strong>Get from Original Post</strong> on a ticket. Reelay doesn’t run speech recognition to make transcripts, so a video posted without captions has none to fetch.</p>' },
  { q: 'Why doesn’t Reelay post to TikTok, Instagram or Snapchat for me?', a: '<p>Reelay prepares the caption and the file for them and you post in their own app, which keeps sounds, tags and Shop links. <strong>Prepare to Publish</strong> checks the file and caption, copies the caption, opens the uploader and shows the video in Finder; then you mark it posted.</p>' },
  { q: 'How do I turn on Bluesky, Threads or Facebook posting?', a: '<p>Connect the account under <strong>Accounts</strong>, switch the platform on under <strong>Settings → Automatic posting</strong>, and restart Reelay. Bluesky and Threads posts go out at their time while Reelay is running and the Mac is awake; Facebook schedules them itself.</p>' },
  { q: 'How do I disconnect an account?', a: `<p>Click <strong>Disconnect</strong> on its card under <strong>Accounts</strong>. Reelay revokes access where the platform allows it, deletes the token from your Keychain and removes the account. See <a href="${href('/data-deletion')}">Data Deletion</a> to remove everything.</p>` },
  { q: 'Can I connect an AI agent?', a: `<p>Yes, through the Agent API on <code>${AGENT_API.host}:${AGENT_API.port}</code>. <strong>Settings → AI agents</strong> shows its address and the access key. See <a href="${href('/ai')}">Agents</a>. An MCP endpoint is planned but isn’t in the app yet.</p>` },
  { q: 'What does Reelay run on?', a: `<p>A Mac with Apple silicon on macOS 12 Monterey or later: that’s the ready-to-run release package. On Windows 10 or 11 you build it yourself with the included PowerShell script, and on Linux you run it from source with Python 3.11 or later. <a href="${href('/download')}">Setup steps</a>.</p>` },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Support: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Interactive Creator Help Center for Reelay Studio: 6-step Quick Tour, 25 visual step-by-step guides across Media Library, The Board, Automations, Accounts & Sign-in, and Video Player."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Creator Help Center">
    <Fragment slot="title">How Reelay works,<br /><span class="text-glow">step by step.</span></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="lede">
      Explore the 6-step studio tour and 25 interactive visual guides mirroring the in-app Help Center.
      <strong>Reviewing Reelay for Google, TikTok or Meta?</strong> Jump to the <a href={href('/reviewers')}>reviewer notes</a> or <a href="#demo-verification">requested permissions</a>.
    </Fragment>

    <div class="help-search-shell">
      <label class="sr-only" for="help-search-input">Search Help Center guides</label>
      <div class="help-search-bar">
        <svg class="help-search-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.75" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" />
          <path d="M13 13l4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" />
        </svg>
        <input
          id="help-search-input"
          class="help-search-input"
          type="search"
          placeholder="Search 25 guides (e.g., YouTube, captions, readiness, TikTok, SQLite)…"
          autocomplete="off"
          data-help-search
        />
        <button type="button" class="help-search-clear" data-help-clear hidden>Clear</button>
      </div>
      <div class="help-search-meta">
        <span data-help-status>Showing all 25 visual guides &amp; 6-step studio tour</span>
        <div class="help-search-actions">
          <button type="button" class="help-action-btn" data-expand-all>Expand all guides</button>
          <button type="button" class="help-action-btn" data-collapse-all>Collapse all</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <!-- 1. TOP CATEGORIES BENTO (6 Primary Topics: 3x2 Desktop, 2x3 Tablet, 1x6 Mobile) -->
  <section class="stage stage--flush-top" aria-label="Primary Help Categories">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="bento" data-reveal>
        {categories.map((cat) => (
          <a class="tile span-2 cat-card" href={`#${cat.id}`}>
            <div class="cat-card-top">
              <span class="cat-num">{cat.number}</span>
              <span class="cat-badge">{cat.badge}</span>
            </div>
            <h3>{cat.title}</h3>
            <p>{cat.blurb}</p>
            <span class="link-more">Explore {cat.title}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. GETTING STARTED: 6-STEP QUICK TOUR + FIRST LAUNCH -->
  <section class="stage stage--lift" id="get-started" aria-labelledby="tour-heading" data-help-section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="chapter-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">00 · Interactive Studio Tour</p>
        <h2 id="tour-heading" class="title" data-pn-label="6-Step Studio Tour">The 6-step loop from import to published.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          New to Reelay on macOS ({RELEASE.requirements})? <a href={href('/download')}>Download Reelay</a>, then open any step below to see what you’re doing, the exact numbered workflow, and the matching studio view.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="guide-stack" data-reveal>
        {tourSteps.map((step, idx) => (
          <details
            class="help-guide"
            id={step.id}
            data-guide-item
            data-search-text={`${step.title} ${step.doing} ${step.steps.join(' ')} ${step.expect} ${step.keywords}`.toLowerCase()}
          >
            <summary class="help-summary">
              <span class="guide-index">0{idx + 1}</span>
              <span class="guide-head-text">
                <strong class="guide-title">{step.title}</strong>
                <span class="guide-subtitle">{step.doing}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="guide-pill">Quick Tour</span>
              <span class="guide-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>

            <div class="help-body">
              <div class="guide-doing-box">
                <span class="doing-kicker">What you’re doing</span>
                <p>{step.doing}</p>
              </div>

              <div class="guide-columns">
                <div class="guide-instructions">
                  <h4 class="guide-subhead">Step-by-step instructions</h4>
                  <ol class="guide-steps">
                    {step.steps.map((s, sIdx) => (
                      <li>
                        <span class="step-num">{sIdx + 1}</span>
                        <span set:html={s} />
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ol>
                  <div class="guide-expect">
                    <strong>What to expect:</strong> {step.expect}
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="guide-media">
                  <figure class="guide-screenshot" data-screen-slot={step.slot}>
                    <picture>
                      <source srcset={`${base}screens/${step.slot}-dark@2x.png`} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
                      <img
                        src={`${base}screens/${step.slot}-light@2x.png`}
                        width="1440"
                        height="900"
                        alt={step.shotAlt}
                        loading="lazy"
                        decoding="async"
                      />
                    </picture>
                    <figcaption>{step.shotAlt}</figcaption>
                  </figure>

                  <div class="video-embed-placeholder" data-video-slot={step.id}>
                    <div class="video-placeholder-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5.5v13l10.5-6.5z" /></svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="video-placeholder-copy">
                      <span class="video-placeholder-kicker">Walkthrough Video Slot</span>
                      <strong>{step.videoTitle || `Walkthrough: ${step.title}`}</strong>
                      <span>Ready for MP4 / YouTube walkthrough embed</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-3" data-reveal>
        <GatekeeperSteps />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. THE 6 PRIMARY CATEGORIES & 25 INTERACTIVE VISUAL GUIDES -->
  {categories.map((cat, cIdx) => (
    <section
      class:list={['stage', { 'stage--lift': cIdx % 2 === 1 }]}
      id={cat.id}
      aria-labelledby={`${cat.id}-heading`}
      data-help-section
    >
      <div class="wrap">
        {cat.id === 'accounts-signin' && (
          <>
            <span id="connecting-youtube" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span id="youtube-setup" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </>
        )}
        <header class="chapter-head" data-reveal>
          <p class="eyebrow">Category {cat.number} · {cat.badge}</p>
          <h2 id={`${cat.id}-heading`} class="title" data-pn-label={cat.title}>{cat.title}</h2>
          <p class="lede">{cat.blurb}</p>
        </header>

        <div class="guide-stack" data-reveal>
          {cat.guides.map((guide, gIdx) => (
            <details
              class="help-guide"
              id={guide.id}
              data-guide-item
              data-aliases={guide.aliases ? guide.aliases.join(',') : undefined}
              data-search-text={`${cat.title} ${guide.title} ${guide.doing} ${guide.steps.join(' ')} ${guide.expect} ${guide.keywords} ${(guide.details || []).map((d) => `${d.title} ${d.lines.join(' ')}`).join(' ')}`.toLowerCase()}
            >
              <summary class="help-summary">
                <span class="guide-index">{cat.number}.{gIdx + 1}</span>
                <span class="guide-head-text">
                  <strong class="guide-title">{guide.title}</strong>
                  <span class="guide-subtitle">{guide.doing}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="guide-pill">{cat.title}</span>
                <span class="guide-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>

              <div class="help-body">
                <div class="guide-doing-box">
                  <span class="doing-kicker">What you’re doing</span>
                  <p>{guide.doing}</p>
                </div>

                <div class="guide-columns">
                  <div class="guide-instructions">
                    <h4 class="guide-subhead">Step-by-step instructions</h4>
                    <ol class="guide-steps">
                      {guide.steps.map((s, sIdx) => (
                        <li>
                          <span class="step-num">{sIdx + 1}</span>
                          <span set:html={s} />
                        </li>
                      ))}
                    </ol>

                    <div class="guide-expect">
                      <strong>What to expect:</strong> {guide.expect}
                    </div>

                    {guide.details && guide.details.length > 0 && (
                      <div class="guide-details-list">
                        {guide.details.map((det) => (
                          <div class="guide-detail-block">
                            <h5>{det.title}</h5>
                            <ul>
                              {det.lines.map((line) => (
                                <li>{line}</li>
                              ))}
                            </ul>
                          </div>
                        ))}
                      </div>
                    )}
                  </div>

                  <div class="guide-media">
                    <figure class="guide-screenshot" data-screen-slot={guide.slot}>
                      <picture>
                        <source srcset={`${base}screens/${guide.slot}-dark@2x.png`} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
                        <img
                          src={`${base}screens/${guide.slot}-light@2x.png`}
                          width="1440"
                          height="900"
                          alt={guide.shotAlt}
                          loading="lazy"
                          decoding="async"
                        />
                      </picture>
                      <figcaption>{guide.shotAlt}</figcaption>
                    </figure>

                    <div class="video-embed-placeholder" data-video-slot={guide.id}>
                      <div class="video-placeholder-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5.5v13l10.5-6.5z" /></svg>
                      </div>
                      <div class="video-placeholder-copy">
                        <span class="video-placeholder-kicker">Walkthrough Video Slot</span>
                        <strong>{guide.videoTitle || `Walkthrough: ${guide.title}`}</strong>
                        <span>Ready for MP4 / YouTube walkthrough embed</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <!-- 4. OAUTH PERMISSIONS & REVIEWER VERIFICATION -->
  <section class="stage stage--lift" id="demo-verification" aria-labelledby="review-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="chapter-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">App review</p>
        <h2 id="review-title" class="title" data-pn-label="Permissions">What Reelay asks each platform for.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The full notes for Google, TikTok and Meta reviewers, with test steps and app IDs, are on the <a href={href('/reviewers')}>reviewer page</a>.</p>
      </header>
      <div data-reveal><PermissionsTable headingLevel={3} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. COMMON QUESTIONS (FAQ) -->
  <section class="stage" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="title" data-reveal>Common Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-2" data-reveal><Faq items={faq} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. CONTACT -->
  <section class="stage stage--tight" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="contact-title" class="title center" data-reveal>Contact</h2>
      <div class="spec-rail mt-2" data-reveal>
        <div class="spec"><span class="spec-label"><strong>Help with the app</strong><a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.support}`}>{CONTACTS.support}</a></span></div>
        <div class="spec"><span class="spec-label"><strong>App review</strong><a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.reviewers}`}>{CONTACTS.reviewers}</a></span></div>
        <div class="spec"><span class="spec-label"><strong>Privacy</strong><a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.privacy}`}>{CONTACTS.privacy}</a></span></div>
        <div class="spec"><span class="spec-label"><strong>Security</strong><a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.security}`}>{CONTACTS.security}</a></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const searchInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-help-search]');
  const clearBtn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-help-clear]');
  const statusEl = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-help-status]');
  const expandAllBtn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-expand-all]');
  const collapseAllBtn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-collapse-all]');
  const guideItems = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-guide-item]')];
  const helpSections = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-help-section]')];

  function filterGuides(rawQuery: string) {
    const words = rawQuery
      .toLowerCase()
      .split(/\s+/)
      .map((w) => w.trim())
      .filter(Boolean);

    if (clearBtn) clearBtn.hidden = words.length === 0;

    if (!words.length) {
      guideItems.forEach((item) => {
        item.hidden = false;
      });
      helpSections.forEach((sec) => {
        sec.hidden = false;
      });
      if (statusEl) {
        statusEl.textContent = 'Showing all 25 visual guides & 6-step studio tour';
      }
      return;
    }

    let matchedCount = 0;
    guideItems.forEach((item) => {
      const hay = item.dataset.searchText || '';
      const hit = words.every((w) => hay.includes(w));
      item.hidden = !hit;
      if (hit) {
        item.open = true;
        matchedCount++;
      }
    });

    helpSections.forEach((sec) => {
      const visibleInSec = sec.querySelectorAll('[data-guide-item]:not([hidden])').length;
      sec.hidden = visibleInSec === 0;
    });

    if (statusEl) {
      statusEl.textContent =
        matchedCount === 0
          ? `No guides matched "${rawQuery.trim()}" — try another keyword like "YouTube", "captions", or "readiness".`
          : `Found ${matchedCount} matching guide${matchedCount === 1 ? '' : 's'} for "${rawQuery.trim()}"`;
    }
  }

  searchInput?.addEventListener('input', () => {
    filterGuides(searchInput.value);
  });

  clearBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!searchInput) return;
    searchInput.value = '';
    filterGuides('');
    searchInput.focus();
  });

  expandAllBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    guideItems.forEach((item) => {
      if (!item.hidden) item.open = true;
    });
  });

  collapseAllBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    guideItems.forEach((item) => {
      item.open = false;
    });
  });

  // Direct URL anchor deep-linking (e.g. /support#connecting-youtube, /support#accounts-connect, /support#auto-rules)
  function openGuideFromHash() {
    const rawHash = window.location.hash.replace(/^#/, '').trim();
    if (!rawHash) return;
    let id = rawHash;
    try {
      id = decodeURIComponent(rawHash);
    } catch {
      id = rawHash;
    }

    // Check direct <details id="..."> match or alias match (e.g. #connecting-youtube -> #accounts-connect)
    const directDetails =
      document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>(`details#${CSS.escape(id)}`) ||
      guideItems.find((item) => (item.dataset.aliases || '').split(',').includes(id));

    if (directDetails) {
      directDetails.hidden = false;
      directDetails.open = true;
      const parentSec = directDetails.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-help-section]');
      if (parentSec) parentSec.hidden = false;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        directDetails.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      });
      return;
    }

    // Check if hash points inside a <details> or to a category section
    const target = document.getElementById(id);
    if (!target) return;
    const parentDetails = target.closest<HTMLDetailsElement>('details.help-guide');
    if (parentDetails) {
      parentDetails.hidden = false;
      parentDetails.open = true;
    }
  }

  openGuideFromHash();
  window.addEventListener('hashchange', openGuideFromHash);
  document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const link = (e.target as Element | null)?.closest?.('a[href*="#"]') as HTMLAnchorElement | null;
    if (!link) return;
    const hrefAttr = link.getAttribute('href') || '';
    const hashIdx = hrefAttr.indexOf('#');
    if (hashIdx === -1) return;
    const hash = hrefAttr.slice(hashIdx + 1);
    if (!hash) return;
    setTimeout(() => openGuideFromHash(), 20);
  });
</script>

